From 5f15a3240bd38cd94a1b61d2f89f572cf7ecd00b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tasker <tasker@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:29:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] hw/audio: move IntelHDAState/IntelHDAStream to
 intel-hda-internal.h

The controller state is private to intel-hda.c; the ACE audio DSP variant
(intel-hda-ace.c, a later patch) needs the streams, the BAR0 container and
the codec bus, so the structures move to an internal header beside the
public one.  intel_hda_update_irq() becomes non-static for the same
reason.  No behaviour change.

Sources studied: QEMU own hw/audio/intel-hda.c only (no external file).
---
 hw/audio/intel-hda-internal.h | 138 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/audio/intel-hda.c          |  95 +----------------------
 2 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 91 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hw/audio/intel-hda-internal.h

diff --git a/hw/audio/intel-hda-internal.h b/hw/audio/intel-hda-internal.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..36ee247be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/hw/audio/intel-hda-internal.h
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
